<description>
Slide each solid rectangular body by the length and direction of its one-cell-thick tail, then redraw the scene with sliders on top.

Input structure
- The background is black.
- Each foreground color represents one object: either a filled rectangle, possibly partly hidden by another color, or a filled rectangle with a straight one-cell-thick tail of length at least two.
- Slider tails extend in one cardinal direction from one side of their rectangle; shifted slider rectangles remain in bounds and do not overlap one another.

Rule
- Restore every non-slider object as the filled rectangle of its input bounding box.
- For every slider, discard the tail and translate only the rectangular body by the tail length in the tail direction.
- Draw the translated slider rectangles over the restored static rectangles.

Key insight
- A thin tail is a displacement vector for its rectangle, while wider missing areas inside another color's bounding box are occlusion that should be restored.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "colored slider objects, each a solid rectangular body with a one-pixel-thick tail",
  "path": "straight in the cardinal direction of the tail for exactly the tail length",
  "trajectory": "move only the solid rectangular body to its final translated bbox; do not leave a trail",
  "transform": "restore non-slider foreground colors as filled rectangles of their input bboxes, erase slider tails, and let translated slider rectangles overwrite restored rectangles"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 20x20, black background
  objects: 3-5 distinct foreground colors; each color is one object
  statics: 1-3 solid filled rectangles, 3-8 rows x 5-9 cols [observed]
  sliders: 2-3 objects, each a solid rectangular body (3-7 rows x 3-9 cols, min dim >= 3) plus a 1-pixel-wide tail
  tail:
    length: 2-6 cells
    direction: any cardinal (R/L/U/D)
    attachment: extends from an interior row/col of the body (never an edge row/col)
  z-order: statics drawn first as full rectangles; slider (body+tail) drawn on top, occluding statics
  occlusion: slider bodies may partially overlap static bboxes in input; statics never overlap each other
  slider constraints:
    body is fully visible (no other color within body region)
    slider bboxes (body+tail) do not overlap each other
    translated body (body shifted by tail_len in tail_dir) stays within grid bounds
    translated bodies do not overlap each other
  output:
    statics restored as full rectangles (un-occluded)
    slider tails erased; bodies translated by tail_length in tail_direction
    translated slider bodies drawn on top of restored statics

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick 3-5 distinct non-black colors; assign 2-3 as sliders, rest as statics
    2. For each slider, choose body dims (3-7 x 3-9, min dim >= 3), a cardinal direction, and tail length 2-6
    3. For each static, choose dims (3-8 x 5-9)
    4. Place all translated slider bodies and static rectangles on the 20x20 grid ensuring no two translated slider bodies overlap and no two statics overlap (statics may underlie translated slider bodies)
    5. For each slider, compute pre-move body position by reversing the translation; choose an interior row/col for the 1-pixel tail; verify body+tail fits in grid and does not overlap other slider bboxes
    6. Render input by drawing statics as full rects first, then each slider body+tail on top
    7. Verify each slider body is fully visible and no static bbox contains background pixels
```
